{
  "result": "Fixed regular source with a large Mobius floor inverse",
  "category": "building-blocks",
  "verifiedAtUtc": "2026-09-11T08:16:23.340249+00:00",
  "statement": "For each real r<2/3, there is f:N->R with |f(q)|<=sqrt(q) and |f(q+1)-f(q)|<=1 for every q, whose sum_(d=1)^N mu(d) f(floor(N/d)) is not eventually O(N^r). The sequence may depend on r.",
  "utility": "Excludes deducing a universal inverse estimate from square-root magnitude and bounded first differences alone.",
  "scope": "A counterexample for auxiliary sequences; no lower bound for the specific centered divisor source H or conclusion about RH.",
  "priority": "Exact mathematical and formalization priority unestablished; no originality or first-formalization claim.",
